# Line endings are normalised to LF everywhere, on every system.
#
# Git for Windows converts text files to CRLF on checkout by default. The
# pipeline templates are embedded in the binary at build time, so a CRLF
# checkout would produce a workflow whose lines end with CRLF from the
# template but with LF inside the multi-line run blocks, which come from Go
# source. The user would be handed a file with mixed line endings, and the
# reference tests in testdata/golden would fail on Windows only.
#
# Keeping everything LF also keeps the recorded act runs in testdata/act
# byte for byte as they were recorded.
* text=auto eol=lf
